<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/knowledge/talks-ted-ai> {
 ex:ted-ai-orchestration a cd:Concept ; skos:prefLabel "Laboratory 5.0: AI builds on explicit interfaces"@en ; cd:hasDefinition ex:ted-ai-definition ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-ai-tools ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-definition a cd:Definition ; cd:body "The AI-assisted workflow layer is under development, not a generally available completed system. The speaker reports successful initial tests: agents construct processing pipelines through documented MCP-accessible operations and those pipelines pass all configured pipeline-validation checks. Complete validation here means the defined structural and semantic checks, not proof of scientific fitness for every analytical task. Standardized names, definitions, ports and constraints constrain tool selection and connections. Planning remains fallible; these early successes do not guarantee hallucination-free planning or validated analytical outcomes. Deterministic execution separately requires suitable implementations and fixed inputs, parameters, versions and seeds where relevant. No success rate, benchmark or independent replication is asserted."@en ; cd:hasSource ex:ted-source-ai-tools ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-points a cd:Interpretation ; cd:body "Constrained planning, explicit validation, reproducible execution."@en ; cd:hasKeyPoint ex:ted-ai-p1, ex:ted-ai-p2, ex:ted-ai-p3 ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-p1 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 1 ; cd:body "**Semantics + algorithms:** documented operations through MCP tools"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-p2 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 2 ; cd:body "**Agent tasks:** create or optimize a processing pipeline"@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-p3 a cd:KeyPoint ; cd:position 3 ; cd:body "==Validate, pin versions, execute; scientific review remains essential=="@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/sources/talks-ted-ai> {
 ex:ted-source-ai-tools a cd:Source ; dct:title "Speaker-described AI workflow orchestration and MCP gateway documentation" ; dct:identifier "speaker-request/laboratory-5.0; stonecastle/cf_service_mcp_server/README.md" ; dct:hasVersion "gateway-readme sha256:8206e1490f6d60e3784d3129deeed5762e2f28c7c65712402efd7a910459ec23" ; dct:description "The speaker describes registered processing steps made callable through MCP for agent-assisted pipeline construction. The inspected gateway README documents a built-in service-call tool with semantic discovery, resolution, validation and invocation. This supports the gateway diagram, not a claim that every operation is a separately enumerated MCP tool or that autonomous scientific planning is error-free. No benchmark or pedagogical-effectiveness evidence is asserted."@en ; cd:supportsResource ex:ted-ai-definition ; cd:authoredResource true .
}
