<https://w3id.org/project-chemie-digital/graph/scenes/talks-ted-ai> {
 ex:ted-scene-ai a cd:SceneDefinition ; cd:focusConcept ex:ted-ai-orchestration ; cd:hasSceneItem ex:ted-ai-heading, ex:ted-ai-diagram, ex:ted-ai-bullets ; cd:narration "This AI-assisted layer is also under development. The speaker reports that first tests already succeed: agents build processing pipelines and those pipelines pass all configured structural and semantic validation checks. This is what complete validation means here, not independent proof that a selected analytical workflow is scientifically appropriate. MCP means Model Context Protocol. The gateway exposes discovery and invocation of documented operations, so the agent can inspect names, definitions, ports and constraints rather than inventing an API. This is useful for complex workflows. The inspected source describes a service-call gateway, not a separately enumerated MCP tool for every operation. Keep planning, validation and execution distinct. Reproducible deterministic execution depends on suitable implementations and fixed data, parameters, software versions and seeds where needed. These controls do not eliminate hallucinations or replace domain review, permissions, failure handling and result checks. The early successes are the speaker's report, without a supplied benchmark, success rate or independent replication; the slide does not claim general availability, autonomous TED-method validation or pedagogical effectiveness."@en ; cd:authoredResource true .
 ex:ted-ai-heading a cd:SceneItem ; cd:position 1 ; cd:selectsResource ex:ted-ai-orchestration ; cd:communicativeRole cd:HeadingRole ; cd:selectionPath "skos:prefLabel@en" ; cd:language "en" ; cd:authoredResource true .
